vkd3d-proton: accept a DXIL hull shader with an implicit pass-through control point phase

A driver that reports shader model 6 receives every fxc (DXBC) shader from
the D3D12 runtime converted to DXIL.  A hull shader whose control point phase
only copies its inputs (fxc drops that phase) comes out with dx.entryPoints
{null, ""}: no entry function and no name.  dxil-spirv converts it (it
synthesizes the pass-through), but vkd3d_shader_compile_dxil() failed the
whole shader with VKD3D_ERROR_INVALID_SHADER when it could not read an entry
name for its quirk lookup, so every tessellation PSO through the AnyOS D3D12
UMD reported DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED.  Without a name the quirk lookup
matches by hash only.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d-shader/dxil.c b/libs/vkd3d-shader/dxil.c
index 6bf14fa..148a460 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d-shader/dxil.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d-shader/dxil.c
@@ -1477,10 +1477,20 @@ int vkd3d_shader_compile_dxil(const struct vkd3d_shader_code *dxbc,
         goto end;
     }
 
+    /* A hull shader whose control point phase is an implicit pass-through
+     * has no entry function: the D3D12 runtime's DXBC->DXIL conversion
+     * (what a driver advertising SM 6 receives for every fxc shader) lists
+     * it in dx.entryPoints with a null function and an empty name.  The
+     * converter handles it (it synthesizes the pass-through); only the
+     * quirk lookup has no name to match. */
     if (dxil_spv_parsed_blob_get_entry_point_demangled_name(blob, 0, &quirk_entry) != DXIL_SPV_SUCCESS)
     {
-        ret = VKD3D_ERROR_INVALID_SHADER;
-        goto end;
+        if (dxil_spv_parsed_blob_get_shader_stage(blob) != DXIL_SPV_STAGE_HULL)
+        {
+            ret = VKD3D_ERROR_INVALID_SHADER;
+            goto end;
+        }
+        quirk_entry = NULL;
     }
 
     quirks = vkd3d_shader_compile_arguments_select_quirks(compiler_args, hash, quirk_entry);
